WEBVTT

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.840
<i>I've been dreaming for a long time.</i>

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:11.350
<i>About being at Nationals</i>

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:13.680
<i>together with Ryuuka and Sara.</i>

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.750
<i>For a long time.</i>

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:29.710
Three Years Ago

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:35.240
Senriyama Middle School

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:35.240
Mahjong Club Room

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.360
I was thinking of doing well in 
the middle school championship

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.260
and going somewhere on a scholarship.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.880
Wow, that's amazing!

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.360
Are you making fun of me?

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.180
Of course not.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.650
Still, that's always felt 
kind of out of my reach.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.140
Once the summer 
tournament is over

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.970
and you choose the school
you want to go to,

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:57.560
maybe I could apply there, too, 
through general admission.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.140
Me, too!

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:00.620
What's with you?

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:12.170
To all the new students!

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:16.620
My name is Atagoma Sae and 
I coach the mahjong club.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:19.600
Practice matches will start right away.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.010
Yes, ma'am!

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:21.850
Listen up.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:24.580
We will be selecting players for regionals

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.100
She's serious.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:27.360
based on the first 
month of practice matches.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.240
In the past, we've had freshmen 
become regular players,

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.960
so I encourage all new members

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:34.650
to be as proactive as possible.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:35.820
Yes, ma'am!

00:01:57.820 --> 00:01:59.620
I didn't make it as a starting player,

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:02.180
but I managed to get onto 
the team as an alternate.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:03.540
That's great!

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:04.600
Congratulations!

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.370
Thanks!

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:10.230
What's more, Ryuuka, 
you've been ranked highly, too.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.460
Slowly, but surely.

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:15.990
I'm hopeless.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:19.660
Based on rankings alone,
 I'm probably in the third group.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.150
You're both guaranteed to be in

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.620
the first group as freshmen. 
That's amazing.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.760
It's just based on the 
first month of matches,

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:27.040
so don't worry about it.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.400
She's right.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:29.870
Thanks.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:34.690
Still, it looks like

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:39.840
we'll have fewer chances to play together.

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:53.780
Toki.

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:56.250
What are you doing?

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.460
I was thinking there might 
be something I could do

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:01.120
to contribute to our club.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:02.260
We'll help you.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:03.480
It's fine.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.370
Why not?

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:07.750
Because I need to make
myself more useful to the club!

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.810
If that makes you feel 
better, than sure.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:13.920
But us helping would be 
your contribution, too.

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:24.980
<i>Absolutely nothing has changed.</i>

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:28.790
<i>They were always my friends.</i>

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:09.120
<i>You're right, Ryuuka.</i>

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:16.370
<b>Round 12:
Promise</b>

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:14.000
<i>Now I'm going to use</i>

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:17.500
<i>the one turn ahead that I got from you.</i>

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:22.170
<i>I'm sorry everyone,</i>

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:25.380
<i>but I'm going to risk it one more time.</i>

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:27.910
Don't!

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:29.890
Stop, Toki!

00:05:40.510 --> 00:05:41.770
<i>Triple...</i>

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:45.180
<i>three turns ahead!</i>

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.110
<i>I saw it.</i>

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:29.170
<i>Riichi.</i>

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.930
<i>I knew that was coming</i>

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:36.220
<i>and that Shindouji's going
 to make a move now.</i>

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:43.940
Pon!

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:48.540
<i>Riichi... you went there.</i>

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:57.990
<i>Triple!</i>

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:03.340
<i>Huh?</i>

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:22.980
<i>Not yet!</i>

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:25.980
<i>Not yet...</i>

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:50.410
<i>Are you coming now, 
Achiga... Matsumi Kuro?</i>

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:00.560
<i>The champion has called a Riichi.</i>

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:04.290
<i>Her next winning hand will be over 18,000.</i>

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:09.010
<i>That's so much. 
I can't play into her hand again.</i>

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:17.980
<i>The 5 of bamboo seems like a dangerous tile.</i>

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:27.460
<i>Tenpai...</i>

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:30.970
<i>I've got a tanyao, pinfu, 
iipeikou, with five dora.</i>

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:33.300
<i>But to get into tenpai,</i>

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:36.970
<i>I'd have to discard a dora.</i>

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:41.210
<i>Try this...</i>

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:43.270
Pon!

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:54.170
<i>That wasn't a ron.</i>

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:55.820
<i>That scared me.</i>

00:09:57.380 --> 00:10:00.500
<i>But it's only a matter of time.</i>

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:03.650
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:06.790
<b>Achiga Girls'</b>

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:07.200
Kuro...

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:09.120
Why didn't she discard a 
safe tile, like a 4 of circles,{pin}

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:11.050
or the 3 of bamboo?

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:13.500
Because Kuro-chan always gets the doras.

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:14.840
I see.

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:17.260
Kuro still has hope.

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:20.010
She hasn't written herself off.

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:21.950
<i>Kuro...</i>

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:36.240
<i>Onjouji-san threw away a 5 of characters</i>

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:37.750
<i>right after a 5 of bamboo.</i>

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:41.270
<i>Could she be trying to increase 
the number of safe tiles?</i>

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:45.540
<i>But the only new safe tile is the</i>

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:48.560
<i>red 5 of characters in my hand.</i>

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:51.690
<i>I should discarded 
the 4 of circles. That's safe.</i>

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:52.780
<i>A dora...</i>

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:55.420
<i>T-throw away a dora?!</i>

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:45.430
<i>That's what happened.</i>

00:11:46.150 --> 00:11:48.780
<i>Those who I had to no 
choice but to part with.</i>

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:55.320
<i>Those who choose to part ways 
in order to move forward.</i>

00:11:57.590 --> 00:11:59.070
<i>Those who see them off.</i>

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:05.660
<i>I was always the waiting type.</i>

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:10.900
<i>But Shizuno-chan and Miss Akado,</i>

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:14.710
<i>Ako-chan and Arata-chan always came back.</i>

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:19.430
<i>Now my sister and I</i>

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:22.430
<i>play together more than 
we ever did before.</i>

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:27.970
<i>I don't know if Nodoka-chan 
will come back,</i>

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:31.840
<i>but we are participating 
in the same festival.</i>

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:39.080
<i>People leave all the time,</i>

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:42.040
<i>so I should have gotten 
used to it by now.</i>

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:53.250
<i>Until now, I've never chosen 
to go a separate way,</i>

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:55.250
<i>but in order to move forward...</i>

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:00.880
<i>...we'll have to separate 
for now!</i>

00:13:04.810 --> 00:13:06.020
Riichi!

00:13:06.020 --> 00:13:07.590
<i>Even if you don't come back,</i>

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:10.770
<i>I'll be waiting.</i>

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:20.580
<i>This is the first time 
a dora has been discarded.</i>

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:21.860
<i>Marvelous.</i>

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:32.650
With a riichi after 
discarding the 8 of circles,

00:13:32.650 --> 00:13:34.200
this would have been it!

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:36.830
Why didn't the champion do that?

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:39.980
With that wait, she'd 
only have the 3 of circles,

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:42.360
as the 6 of circles and 
the north are all out.

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:44.330
After her analysis of the players in

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:47.060
East Hand 1 of the first 
half of the match,

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:49.130
she decided that Achiga's Matsumi Kuro

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:51.210
would never discard a dora.

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:55.110
However, people surpass your expectations.

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:04.400
Pon.

00:14:09.190 --> 00:14:10.660
<i>Transformation complete.</i>

00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:12.660
<i>Good work.</i>

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:19.120
<i>Usually, my tactic would
 be to evade,</i>

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:21.180
<i>but there's someone I want to
 take down a peg or two.</i>

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:24.710
<i>How nice of her to declare riichi.</i>

00:14:43.680 --> 00:14:45.320
<i>That's right, Champion.</i>

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:49.990
<i>That's Achiga's winning tile.</i>

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:57.040
Ron!

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:01.540
Mentanpin, iipeiko, and six dora.

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:01.540
[Mentanpin - riichi + tanyao + pinfu]

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:05.550
16,000 plus the bonus...

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:09.800
that's 16,600 points.

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:18.310
That's the end of the first players' match!

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:23.190
A champion hasn't played into 
a hand this big in decades!

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:24.880
I think it's more like two years.

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:25.980
I suppose you're right.

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:28.740
Back in high school,

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:30.830
I also once played into a hand that

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:33.030
was more expensive than a haneman.

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:34.630
That also resulted from someone's

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:36.880
playing style surpassing
all my predictions.

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:39.500
The memory has stayed with 
me strongly all this time.

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:42.050
You did it, Kuro-san!

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:43.100
Yeah!

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:44.280
<i>Back when I was playing,</i>

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:46.080
<i>it would've never occurred
to me to work together</i>

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:47.580
<i>with two other players.</i>

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:51.130
<i>Or even to throw away a part 
of myself on a gamble.</i>

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:54.960
<i>You really did well, Kuro.</i>

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:07.270
<i>I did end up losing points again,</i>

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:11.030
<i>but I have a lot more points 
now than in the second round match</i>

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:13.460
<i>to hand over to my sister.</i>

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:16.520
Good game.

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:21.790
Good game.

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:25.970
That was marvelous.

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:33.430
Senriyama.

00:16:38.040 --> 00:16:39.700
Onjouji-san!

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:48.360
Good... game.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:49.480
Are you all right?

00:16:57.710 --> 00:16:59.620
I'm fine.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:01.120
I'm just faking it.

00:17:01.690 --> 00:17:04.540
Don't worry about me.

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:30.440
Onjouji-san!

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:31.900
Hang on!

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:33.530
Toki!

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:35.780
Ryuuka...

00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:37.450
Toki!

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:40.160
Toki!

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:43.990
The floor here is colder than at school.

00:17:46.720 --> 00:17:48.170
Hang in there Toki!

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:51.330
It's not such a big deal...

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:52.700
Don't talk!

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:54.170
Better to be safe!

00:17:54.810 --> 00:17:56.600
I'm so sorry.

00:17:56.600 --> 00:18:00.430
I lost all those points, and now this.

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:02.910
We'll take care of it.

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:04.430
Just leave it to us.

00:18:05.540 --> 00:18:06.940
The second players' match...

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:09.430
Go, Izumi!

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:12.570
Right! You can count on me.

00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:22.300
You think Onjouji-san's 
going to be okay?

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:25.080
I guess she wasn't faking it.

00:18:26.860 --> 00:18:30.380
The semifinals will resume shortly.

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:34.000
We ask that participating players please 
make their way to the competition hall.

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:36.120
Yuu-san, it's time to go.

00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:48.730
Shizu, what's wrong?

00:18:56.100 --> 00:18:58.240
What is she doing here?

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:01.570
Nodoka!

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:03.200
Nodoka?

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:07.120
What's wrong, Nodo-chan?

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:16.350
Shizuno... Ako... Kuro-san...

00:19:17.610 --> 00:19:19.290
It's been so long!

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:20.650
Nodoka-chan.

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:24.460
You know these girls?

00:19:24.460 --> 00:19:27.020
These are some friends from 
back when I was in Nara.

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:28.810
It's been three years.

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:32.150
Nodoka, you're not 
playing today, are you?

00:19:32.430 --> 00:19:34.710
I actually came to watch the match today,

00:19:34.710 --> 00:19:36.950
but the auditorium was full.

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:39.760
Then this lady from the press said
I could watch from the press room.

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:42.380
What? What's your relationship!? 
Tell me everything!

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:44.890
Wow, I guess that's a 
star player for you.

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:48.930
Nodoka, we're definitely going 
to be in the final round.

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:50.540
You've got to be there, too!

00:19:51.310 --> 00:19:53.540
I can't promise something like that,

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:57.300
but I will do everything 
I can to be there.

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:01.050
Then, see you at the finals!

00:20:02.170 --> 00:20:03.220
Yes!

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:06.370
Hey, hey!

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:10.150
Come on...!

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:13.620
Shizu...

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:19.830
Shizu, is that okay?

00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:21.650
Sure.

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:27.050
'Cause we're definitely going to win!

00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:05.950
<b>Time until Hand 2 begins:</b>

00:22:08.370 --> 00:22:09.620
I'm off!

00:22:09.620 --> 00:22:10.680
Go get 'em!

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:12.020
Give it your best, Yuu-nee!

00:22:12.020 --> 00:22:13.390
Go get 'em, onee-chan!

00:22:13.390 --> 00:22:14.230
Yuu-san...

00:22:17.300 --> 00:22:18.490
<i>Senpai...</i>

00:22:20.590 --> 00:22:22.480
You did good, Hanada.

00:22:22.810 --> 00:22:26.110
No, I just did all I could.

00:22:26.640 --> 00:22:28.750
Yoshiko, you're up.

00:22:29.240 --> 00:22:30.140
All right!

00:22:30.140 --> 00:22:32.280
Do your best, senpai.

00:22:42.230 --> 00:22:45.660
And now it's finally time 
to resume the game!

00:22:45.660 --> 00:22:49.050
All the second players have made 
their way to the competition hall!

00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:54.450
The gong for the fight 
will ring any moment now!

00:23:01.910 --> 00:23:03.660
I wonder if it's over.

00:23:10.160 --> 00:23:12.120
In the 21st century,

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:14.200
the number of mahjong players around

00:23:14.200 --> 00:23:17.410
the world is in the hundreds of millions,

00:23:17.410 --> 00:23:19.960
and the professional players 
have an avid following.

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:21.750
Even at the high school level,

00:23:21.750 --> 00:23:25.420
a large-scale national tournament 
is held every year.

00:23:25.420 --> 00:23:29.760
That's where the high 
school players compete

00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:33.010
in order to make it into the 
league of professionals.

00:23:33.760 --> 00:23:38.850
This is the path of the girls 
who were aiming for the top.

00:23:53.520 --> 00:23:55.390
The second players' match of the

00:23:55.390 --> 00:23:58.790
Block A semifinals of the
National Championship has begun.
